WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.768
It was hard not to be

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.236
fixated on the drama

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.037
that unfolded

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.505
in the House of Representatives

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.339
this week,

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.674
where the Republican Party

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.175
had a nervous breakdown

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.511
in full public view.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.680
This crisis was entirely of the

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.348
party's own making.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.116
For decades,

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.317
it has whipped its base

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.085
into a righteous fury

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.221
by promising radical policies

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.256
that offer emotional satisfaction

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.391
to their hard line

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.558
constituents,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.559
from rolling back

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.561
Medicare and Social Security

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.563
to defaulting on the national debt

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.799
to eliminating whole government agencies.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.135
But because these policies

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.870
are totally unworkable,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.638
they never happen.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.874
The lesson that the base has internalized

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:41.708
is that it

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.376
was constantly being betrayed

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.478
by cowardly moderates.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.514
The solution now is to maintain

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.748
a permanent vise

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.116
grip on the speaker,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.052
ensuring that he will always do

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.087
what the hard liners want.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.322
This is, as many have noted, a recipe

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.124
for permanent blackmail and

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.492
constant chaos.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.561
The Republican

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.296
Party's troubles are severe.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.031
Newt Gingrich told Axios

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.632
that the party

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.933
is in its worst shape

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.569
in almost six decades.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.071
But it is not alone.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.239
In many countries around the world.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.542
Populists are flailing.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.744
Look at Britain, where Brexit, perhaps

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.680
the ultimate 21st century populist cause,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.315
has caused havoc

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.117
within the Conservative Party,

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.351
which used to be described

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.352
as the world's oldest

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.388
and most successful political party.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.989
Britain has had

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.624
five prime ministers

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.793
in the six years since 2016.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:34.928
The prior

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.362
five prime ministers

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:39.032
spend more than 30 years

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.201
The self-defeating decision to exit

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.735
its largest market,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.170
the European Union,

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.172
continues to depress the country's

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.640
economic prospects

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.174
and Britain

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.910
remains the weakest of the G7 economies

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.779
in the G20.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.248
Only Russia is projected to do worse than

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.483
Britain in the near future.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.986
The story is similar in South America,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.187
even though that continent

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.989
has been swept up in populism

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.991
from both the right and the left.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.594
Neither version is doing very well

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.328
in Brazil.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.496
Jair Bolsonaro

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.564
lost his bid for reelection,

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.298
but the winner,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.133
former President

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.802
Lula, will also find it hard to implement

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.271
some of his more radical promises

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.172
in Chile.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.974
Left wing populist coalesced

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:21.774
around a plan

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.243
to completely redo

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.078
the country's constitution,

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.613
putting forward a new one

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:29.149
that even many Left-Of-Center politicians

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.518
regarded as extreme and unworkable.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.953
In the ensuing referendum,

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.156
86% of Chileans turned out

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.491
rejecting the new constitution

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.560
by a whopping 62%.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.862
On the other side of the globe

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:43.930
in Australia,

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.198
right wing politicians

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.366
had embraced Trump's

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.535
style policies and rhetoric.

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:50.170
Under Prime Minister Scott Morrison,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.571
they spoke a language

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.238
that mirrored

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.973
the grievance politics of older

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.008
white voters

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.276
and scared the country

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.444
about the dangers of immigration, crime

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.345
and so-called

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.480
African gangs

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.015
that were supposedly marauding

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.917
through Victoria.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.185
But he bungled the COVID

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.920
pandemic and had little success

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.087
with the economy.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.689
In the recent elections,

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.658
Australia's conservatives suffered

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.860
their worst loss ever

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.161
and the even more extreme

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.196
united Australia

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.830
and One Nation parties

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.566
did poorly as well.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.667
The new Labor Prime

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.402
Minister currently enjoys

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.671
an extraordinarily high approval rating

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.641
Why is this happening?

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.343
Well, populism thrives

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.011
as an opposition movement.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.913
It denounces the establishment,

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.281
encourages fears

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.783
and conspiracy theories

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.152
about nefarious ruling elites

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:39.886
and promises

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.588
emotional responses

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.890
rather than actual programs.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.491
For example, build a wall.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.493
Pandemic nation. Stop trade.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.696
But once in government,

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.264
the shallowness of these policy

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.932
proposals is exposed,

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.335
and leaders can't blame others as easily.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:56.502
Meanwhile,

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.005
if non populist forces are sensible

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.840
and actually get things done,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.942
they defang some of the populist right.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.310
Look at America,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.311
where Joe Biden's

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.512
moderate style,

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.747
serious demeanor

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.849
and practical policymaking

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.251
have given him large

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.086
legislative accomplishments

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.554
without triggering a massive

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.389
electoral backlash.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.523
Now he benefits

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.826
by being an old white man.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:20.960
Had Barack Obama

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.296
enacted the same policies as Joe Biden?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.664
I have a feeling

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.532
we would hear much more talk

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.268
of his dangerous socialism

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.103
and un-American policies,

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.071
complete with racial innuendos.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.340
The poster child

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.909
for populism has always been Argentina.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.211
Juan Peron

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.480
and his even more charismatic wife, Eva,

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.782
built a powerful mass movement

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.417
that attacked the old elites

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.618
and promised to become

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.387
the voice of the people.

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.221
In fact,

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.490
they destroyed Argentina's economy.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.357
What had once been

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.292
one of the world's

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.360
wealthiest countries in the 19 tens

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.729
was only a few decades later,

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.631
a basket case economy.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.599
Ever since

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:00.833
Argentine populists

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.568
have promised voters, the moon

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.370
ran up staggering debts

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.372
and then routinely defaulted.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.075
But now things have soured for them,

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.144
prompting the Economist to observe

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.211
that Argentina's

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:15.381
populist movement is at its lowest ebb.

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.251
Former President Eduardo Holiday

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:19.686
told the magazine

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.655
terrorism is obviously the main culprit

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.856
for the situation.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.224
Of Argentina,

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:28.728
saying today we are in our worst moment.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.798
These trends are not permanent.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.666
The world's complicated problems

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.734
always allow for

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.636
someone who proposes answers

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.572
that are simple, seductive and wrong.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.975
But let us hope that 2023 will see

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:46.379
populism exposed for the sham that it is.

